name>MAKINO, KENJIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SOEDA, KOUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKIMOTO, MASAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUKADA, KAZUHISA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process for producing a dispersant for use in powdery hydraulic compositions, which comprises adding a reducing agent to a liquid consisting mainly of a polycarboxylic acid polymer having a polyalkylene glycol chain and subsequently drying and powdering the mixture; a powdery hydraulic composition obtained by the process; and a hydraulic composition obtained therefrom.  The dispersant is satisfactory in flowability and dispersing ability and can be added beforehand to a cement, etc.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un procédé de production d'un dispersant pour composition hydraulique en poudre consistant à ajouter un agent réducteur à un liquide comprenant principalement un polymère d'acide carboxylique à chaîne polyalkylène glycol, puis à dessécher puis pulvériser le mélange. L'invention porte en outre sur la composition hydraulique en poudre ainsi obtenue, et sur la composition hydraulique en étant tirée. Le dispersant satisfaisant du point de vue de la fluidité et de la capacité de dispersion peut s'ajouter préalablement à du ciment, etc.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of th